{"id": 1, "ok": true, "cmd": "mma", "ucas": "mma m16n8k8 f16 model rdna2 nofile", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "mma", "shape": "m16n8k8", "accumulator": "f16", "model": "rdna2", "tried": 1768, "dataflows": [{"cost": 73.75, "dataflow": "output-stationary; A: 8 quad broadcasts; B: 8 loads from shared memory (register-major); 16 fdot2", "depth": 8}, {"cost": 73.75, "dataflow": "output-stationary; A: 8 quad broadcasts; B: 8 loads from shared memory (lane-major); 16 fdot2", "depth": 8}, {"cost": 75, "dataflow": "output-stationary; A: 6 xor shuffles; B: 8 shuffles; 16 fdot2; k order by lane", "depth": 8}, {"cost": 88.75, "dataflow": "output-stationary; A: 4 loads from shared memory (register-major), 4 xor shuffles; B: 4 loads from shared memory (register-major), 4 xor shuffles; 16 fdot2", "depth": 8}, {"cost": 88.75, "dataflow": "output-stationary; A: 4 loads from shared memory (register-major), 4 xor shuffles; B: 4 loads from shared memory (lane-major), 4 xor shuffles; 16 fdot2", "depth": 8}, {"cost": 91.75, "dataflow": "output-stationary; A: 4 loads from shared memory (register-major), 4 xor shuffles; B: 4 xor shuffles, 4 shuffles; 16 fdot2", "depth": 8}], "reference_cost": 75, "chosen": "output-stationary; A: 8 quad broadcasts; B: 8 loads from shared memory (register-major); 16 fdot2", "cost": 73.75, "bound": "gamma_8 (sum_k |A_ik B_kj| + |C_ij|) + f16 rounding", "depth": 8, "glsl": "// D = A B + C on a warp's fragments as PTX's mma.sync.aligned.m16n8k8.row.col\n// lays them out (f16 A and B, f16 C and D), for a GPU without a matrix unit.\n// ucas mma m16n8k8 f16 under rdna2: output-stationary; A: 8 quad broadcasts; B: 8 loads from shared memory (register-major); 16 fdot2;\n// cost 73.75 (each word fetched from its lane: 75).\n// Proved over the 32 lanes: each element of D is its 8 products and C, each once;\n// |D - (A B + C)| <= gamma_8 (sum_k |A_ik B_kj| + |C_ij|), then D's f16 rounding, u = 2^-24.\n#extension GL_KHR_shader_subgroup_basic : require\n#extension GL_KHR_shader_subgroup_shuffle : require\n#extension GL_KHR_shader_subgroup_quad : require\n#extension GL_EXT_spirv_intrinsics : require\n#extension GL_EXT_shader_explicit_arithmetic_types_float16 : require\n// OpFDot2MixAcc32VALVE: a.x * b.x + a.y * b.y + c in f32\nspirv_instruction(extensions = [\"SPV_VALVE_mixed_float_dot_product\"], capabilities = [6912], id = 6916)\nfloat mma_fdot2(f16vec2 a, f16vec2 b, float c);\n#ifndef MMA_WARPS\n#define MMA_WARPS 1  // the workgroup's warps of 32\n#endif\nshared uint mma_slot[MMA_WARPS * 96u];\nvoid mma_m16n8k8_f16(uint a[2], uint b[1], uint c[2], out uint d[2])\n{\n\tuint lane = gl_SubgroupInvocationID & 31u;\n\tuint base = gl_SubgroupInvocationID & ~31u;\n\tuint slot = (gl_LocalInvocationIndex >> 5) * 96u;\n\tsubgroupBarrier();\n\tuint v1 = b[0];\n\tuint a0 = slot + (lane ^ 64u);\n\tmma_slot[a0] = v1;\n\tsubgroupBarrier();\n\tuint v4 = c[0];\n\tfloat v5 = unpackHalf2x16(v4).x;\n\tfloat v6 = unpackHalf2x16(v4).y;\n\tuint v7 = c[1];\n\tfloat v8 = unpackHalf2x16(v7).x;\n\tfloat v9 = unpackHalf2x16(v7).y;\n\tuint v10 = a[0];\n\tuint v11 = subgroupQuadBroadcast(v10, 0u);\n\tuint a2 = slot + (((lane & 3u) << 3u) ^ 64u);\n\tuint v12 = mma_slot[a2];\n\tfloat v13 = mma_fdot2(unpackFloat2x16(v11), unpackFloat2x16(v12), v5);\n\tuint v14 = mma_slot[a2 + 4u];\n\tfloat v15 = mma_fdot2(unpackFloat2x16(v11), unpackFloat2x16(v14), v6);\n\tuint v16 = a[1];\n\tuint v17 = subgroupQuadBroadcast(v16, 0u);\n\tfloat v18 = mma_fdot2(unpackFloat2x16(v17), unpackFloat2x16(v12), v8);\n\tfloat v19 = mma_fdot2(unpackFloat2x16(v17), unpackFloat2x16(v14), v9);\n\tuint v20 = subgroupQuadBroadcast(v10, 1u);\n\tuint v21 = mma_slot[a2 + 1u];\n\tfloat v22 = mma_fdot2(unpackFloat2x16(v20), unpackFloat2x16(v21), v13);\n\tuint v23 = mma_slot[a2 + 5u];\n\tfloat v24 = mma_fdot2(unpackFloat2x16(v20), unpackFloat2x16(v23), v15);\n\tuint v25 = subgroupQuadBroadcast(v16, 1u);\n\tfloat v26 = mma_fdot2(unpackFloat2x16(v25), unpackFloat2x16(v21), v18);\n\tfloat v27 = mma_fdot2(unpackFloat2x16(v25), unpackFloat2x16(v23), v19);\n\tuint v28 = subgroupQuadBroadcast(v10, 2u);\n\tuint v29 = mma_slot[a2 + 2u];\n\tfloat v30 = mma_fdot2(unpackFloat2x16(v28), unpackFloat2x16(v29), v22);\n\tuint v31 = mma_slot[a2 + 6u];\n\tfloat v32 = mma_fdot2(unpackFloat2x16(v28), unpackFloat2x16(v31), v24);\n\tuint v33 = subgroupQuadBroadcast(v16, 2u);\n\tfloat v34 = mma_fdot2(unpackFloat2x16(v33), unpackFloat2x16(v29), v26);\n\tfloat v35 = mma_fdot2(unpackFloat2x16(v33), unpackFloat2x16(v31), v27);\n\tuint v36 = subgroupQuadBroadcast(v10, 3u);\n\tuint v37 = mma_slot[a2 + 3u];\n\tfloat v38 = mma_fdot2(unpackFloat2x16(v36), unpackFloat2x16(v37), v30);\n\tuint v39 = mma_slot[a2 + 7u];\n\tfloat v40 = mma_fdot2(unpackFloat2x16(v36), unpackFloat2x16(v39), v32);\n\tuint v41 = subgroupQuadBroadcast(v16, 3u);\n\tfloat v42 = mma_fdot2(unpackFloat2x16(v41), unpackFloat2x16(v37), v34);\n\tfloat v43 = mma_fdot2(unpackFloat2x16(v41), unpackFloat2x16(v39), v35);\n\td[0] = packHalf2x16(vec2(v38, v40));\n\td[1] = packHalf2x16(vec2(v42, v43));\n}\n", "whatif_wide_cost": 55.75}, "notes": [], "conditions": ["every lane of the warp active, the warp a subgroup of 32 or 32 aligned lanes of a larger one", "the f32 sums round to nearest", "an fdot2 rounds at most twice (SPV_VALVE_mixed_float_dot_product leaves its rounding to the device)"], "checks": [{"kind": "random", "points": 8192, "max_diff": 0.9852951443201818, "passed": true, "text": "random fragments against the exact sums, as a fraction of the bound"}], "proof": {"kind": "exhaustive", "text": "the plan run on symbols in all 32 lanes: every element of D is exactly its K products and its C, each once"}, "files": [], "text": "mma m16n8k8: D = A B + C on a warp's fragments as PTX's mma.sync.aligned.m16n8k8.row.col lays them out, f16 A and B, f16 C and D, 32 lanes, under rdna2 (1768 dataflows tried)\n  each of D's 128 elements is a sum of 8 products of f16 and its C\n   1. 73.75     output-stationary; A: 8 quad broadcasts; B: 8 loads from shared memory (register-major); 16 fdot2, depth 8\n   2. 73.75     output-stationary; A: 8 quad broadcasts; B: 8 loads from shared memory (lane-major); 16 fdot2, depth 8\n   3. 75        output-stationary; A: 6 xor shuffles; B: 8 shuffles; 16 fdot2; k order by lane, depth 8\n   4. 88.75     output-stationary; A: 4 loads from shared memory (register-major), 4 xor shuffles; B: 4 loads from shared memory (register-major), 4 xor shuffles; 16 fdot2, depth 8\n   5. 88.75     output-stationary; A: 4 loads from shared memory (register-major), 4 xor shuffles; B: 4 loads from shared memory (lane-major), 4 xor shuffles; 16 fdot2, depth 8\n   6. 91.75     output-stationary; A: 4 loads from shared memory (register-major), 4 xor shuffles; B: 4 xor shuffles, 4 shuffles; 16 fdot2, depth 8\n  (30 more: mma ... all)\n  B-stationary: none possible: no assignment of the partial sums to registers (a xor of the lane's bits) lets a butterfly send and read them from the same registers in every lane\n  reference, each word fetched from the lane that holds it: 75 (output-stationary; A: 8 quad broadcasts; B: 8 shuffles; 16 fdot2, depth 8); the chosen is 1.02x cheaper\n  chosen: output-stationary; A: 8 quad broadcasts; B: 8 loads from shared memory (register-major); 16 fdot2, cost 73.75\n    8 exchanges, 8 loads and 1 stores of shared memory (bank conflicts at most 1-way), 2 barriers, 4 unpacks, 16 fdot2, 0 adds, 2 packs\n  proof: the plan run on symbols in all 32 lanes gives every element of D as exactly its 8 products and its C, each once (exhaustive over the lanes)\n  bound: |D - (A B + C)| <= gamma_8 (sum_k |A_ik B_kj| + |C_ij|), gamma_8 = 8 u / (1 - 8 u) = 4.768e-07, u = 2^-24; then D's f16 rounding, 2^-11 |D| (2^-25 below the normals)\n    a product of two f16 is exact in f32 (22 significant bits, exponents within f32's normals), so only the sums round: each term through at most 8 roundings (an fdot2 counted as two)\n  holds when: every lane of the warp active, the warp a subgroup of 32 or 32 aligned lanes of a larger one; the f32 sums round to nearest; an fdot2 rounds at most twice (SPV_VALVE_mixed_float_dot_product leaves its rounding to the device)\n  check: 64 random sets of fragments in f32 against the exact sums: within the bound, the largest error 0.985 of the bound (sampled, not a proof)\n  GLSL (mma_m16n8k8_f16.glsl):\n    // D = A B + C on a warp's fragments as PTX's mma.sync.aligned.m16n8k8.row.col\n    // lays them out (f16 A and B, f16 C and D), for a GPU without a matrix unit.\n    // ucas mma m16n8k8 f16 under rdna2: output-stationary; A: 8 quad broadcasts; B: 8 loads from shared memory (register-major); 16 fdot2;\n    // cost 73.75 (each word fetched from its lane: 75).\n    // Proved over the 32 lanes: each element of D is its 8 products and C, each once;\n    // |D - (A B + C)| <= gamma_8 (sum_k |A_ik B_kj| + |C_ij|), then D's f16 rounding, u = 2^-24.\n    #extension GL_KHR_shader_subgroup_basic : require\n    #extension GL_KHR_shader_subgroup_shuffle : require\n    #extension GL_KHR_shader_subgroup_quad : require\n    #extension GL_EXT_spirv_intrinsics : require\n    #extension GL_EXT_shader_explicit_arithmetic_types_float16 : require\n    // OpFDot2MixAcc32VALVE: a.x * b.x + a.y * b.y + c in f32\n    spirv_instruction(extensions = [\"SPV_VALVE_mixed_float_dot_product\"], capabilities = [6912], id = 6916)\n    float mma_fdot2(f16vec2 a, f16vec2 b, float c);\n    #ifndef MMA_WARPS\n    #define MMA_WARPS 1  // the workgroup's warps of 32\n    #endif\n    shared uint mma_slot[MMA_WARPS * 96u];\n    void mma_m16n8k8_f16(uint a[2], uint b[1], uint c[2], out uint d[2])\n    {\n    \tuint lane = gl_SubgroupInvocationID & 31u;\n    \tuint base = gl_SubgroupInvocationID & ~31u;\n    \tuint slot = (gl_LocalInvocationIndex >> 5) * 96u;\n    \tsubgroupBarrier();\n    \tuint v1 = b[0];\n    \tuint a0 = slot + (lane ^ 64u);\n    \tmma_slot[a0] = v1;\n    \tsubgroupBarrier();\n    \tuint v4 = c[0];\n    \tfloat v5 = unpackHalf2x16(v4).x;\n    \tfloat v6 = unpackHalf2x16(v4).y;\n    \tuint v7 = c[1];\n    \tfloat v8 = unpackHalf2x16(v7).x;\n    \tfloat v9 = unpackHalf2x16(v7).y;\n    \tuint v10 = a[0];\n    \tuint v11 = subgroupQuadBroadcast(v10, 0u);\n    \tuint a2 = slot + (((lane & 3u) << 3u) ^ 64u);\n    \tuint v12 = mma_slot[a2];\n    \tfloat v13 = mma_fdot2(unpackFloat2x16(v11), unpackFloat2x16(v12), v5);\n    \tuint v14 = mma_slot[a2 + 4u];\n    \tfloat v15 = mma_fdot2(unpackFloat2x16(v11), unpackFloat2x16(v14), v6);\n    \tuint v16 = a[1];\n    \tuint v17 = subgroupQuadBroadcast(v16, 0u);\n    \tfloat v18 = mma_fdot2(unpackFloat2x16(v17), unpackFloat2x16(v12), v8);\n    \tfloat v19 = mma_fdot2(unpackFloat2x16(v17), unpackFloat2x16(v14), v9);\n    \tuint v20 = subgroupQuadBroadcast(v10, 1u);\n    \tuint v21 = mma_slot[a2 + 1u];\n    \tfloat v22 = mma_fdot2(unpackFloat2x16(v20), unpackFloat2x16(v21), v13);\n    \tuint v23 = mma_slot[a2 + 5u];\n    \tfloat v24 = mma_fdot2(unpackFloat2x16(v20), unpackFloat2x16(v23), v15);\n    \tuint v25 = subgroupQuadBroadcast(v16, 1u);\n    \tfloat v26 = mma_fdot2(unpackFloat2x16(v25), unpackFloat2x16(v21), v18);\n    \tfloat v27 = mma_fdot2(unpackFloat2x16(v25), unpackFloat2x16(v23), v19);\n    \tuint v28 = subgroupQuadBroadcast(v10, 2u);\n    \tuint v29 = mma_slot[a2 + 2u];\n    \tfloat v30 = mma_fdot2(unpackFloat2x16(v28), unpackFloat2x16(v29), v22);\n    \tuint v31 = mma_slot[a2 + 6u];\n    \tfloat v32 = mma_fdot2(unpackFloat2x16(v28), unpackFloat2x16(v31), v24);\n    \tuint v33 = subgroupQuadBroadcast(v16, 2u);\n    \tfloat v34 = mma_fdot2(unpackFloat2x16(v33), unpackFloat2x16(v29), v26);\n    \tfloat v35 = mma_fdot2(unpackFloat2x16(v33), unpackFloat2x16(v31), v27);\n    \tuint v36 = subgroupQuadBroadcast(v10, 3u);\n    \tuint v37 = mma_slot[a2 + 3u];\n    \tfloat v38 = mma_fdot2(unpackFloat2x16(v36), unpackFloat2x16(v37), v30);\n    \tuint v39 = mma_slot[a2 + 7u];\n    \tfloat v40 = mma_fdot2(unpackFloat2x16(v36), unpackFloat2x16(v39), v32);\n    \tuint v41 = subgroupQuadBroadcast(v16, 3u);\n    \tfloat v42 = mma_fdot2(unpackFloat2x16(v41), unpackFloat2x16(v37), v34);\n    \tfloat v43 = mma_fdot2(unpackFloat2x16(v41), unpackFloat2x16(v39), v35);\n    \td[0] = packHalf2x16(vec2(v38, v40));\n    \td[1] = packHalf2x16(vec2(v42, v43));\n    }\n  (nofile: mma_m16n8k8_f16.glsl, 3524 bytes, checksum 91a57f44)\n  what if: were a 64- or 128-bit shared access priced as one 32-bit access (load_shared_x2, load_shared_x4, store_shared_x2, store_shared_x4, which rdna2 does not list): 55.75, 1.32x cheaper (output-stationary; A: 8 quad broadcasts; B: 8 loads from shared memory (register-major, in 2 wide accesses); 16 fdot2)\n"}
